**Theorem (`decodeList_encodeList`).** Decoding the code of a finite list recovers the list.

*Proof.* Induction on the list or code uses the successor coding equation and the fact that unpairing a freshly paired head and tail recovers both components. ∎

**Theorem (`reForallStp_eq`).** Unpacking one universal-witness step yields the update that consumes the next witness and list entry.

*Proof.* Unpairing the current list entry, witness code and flag gives exactly the unpacked witness-checking update. ∎

**Theorem (`reForallChar_eq`).** The coded universal-witness characteristic is the final flag of the corresponding fold over the decoded list.

*Proof.* The coded-fold equation turns the packed step into the unpacked witness-checking update over the decoded list. ∎

**Theorem (`reForallF_foldl_eq_one_iff`).** The characteristic value is one exactly when every finite condition encoded in its arguments holds.

*Proof.* Induction on the candidate list tracks the binary flag and aligns each entry with the same-position witness obtained by decoding the witness code. ∎

**Theorem (`reForallChar_eq_one_iff`).** The characteristic value is one exactly when every finite condition encoded in its arguments holds.

*Proof.* Specializing the fold characterization to initial flag one leaves exactly the pointwise witness checks below the decoded length. ∎

